@ # Transclusion fixture

A tiny document in the *Markdown* dialect that exercises transclusion (§10). The
title, an intro, and the source section all live in one `@` chunk, so the node
boundary is the markdown heading, not the chunk. A later section pulls the source
in with `\transclude`, so the weave must cut the node at the heading, splice it in
place, scope its ids, and link back to it.

## The source {#sec:source}

This section is the transclusion target. The title above it belongs to a
shallower node, so the copy must start here and leave the `h1` out. It owns a
small code chunk, so the transcluded copy must scope a code section's id too.

<<demo.rs>>=
pub fn demo() -> u32 {
    7
}
@ ## The reuse {#sec:reuse}

The source section appears again here, transcluded in place:

\transclude{sec:source}

The document continues after the copy.
